internal/gitignore vendors the gitignore pattern matcher from go-git
(https://github.com/go-git/go-git), taken from module
github.com/go-git/go-git/v6 at v6.0.0-alpha.5, package
plumbing/format/gitignore. go-git is distributed under the Apache License 2.0,
the same license as Strument; the LICENSE file at the repository root applies.

The package code carries its own upstream attribution, reproduced from doc.go:

    Copyright (c) Oleg Sklyar, Silvertern and source{d}

    The package code was donated to source{d} to include, modify and develop
    further as a part of the `go-git` project, release it on the license of
    the whole project or delete it from the project.

Files taken verbatim, unmodified:

  * doc.go       — package documentation and the gitignore pattern spec
  * pattern.go   — ParsePattern and the wildmatch implementation ported from
                   Git 2.54.0 (handles **, character classes, POSIX classes)
  * matcher.go   — NewMatcher and priority resolution

Strument's additions and omissions:

  * dir.go is NOT vendored. Upstream reads ignore files through the go-billy
    filesystem abstraction (github.com/go-git/go-billy), which Strument does not
    depend on and does not want to add, and it eagerly recurses the entire
    worktree. read.go replaces it: the same line filtering (skip comments and
    blank lines, hand the rest to ParsePattern) over os, exposed per directory
    so a caller walking the tree collects patterns as it descends rather than
    traversing twice.

  * Global and system patterns (core.excludesFile from ~/.gitconfig and
    /etc/gitconfig) are not read. Upstream reaches them through go-git's
    gitconfig decoder, a larger dependency than the matcher itself, and a
    per-user ignore file should not silently change which files Strument will
    show a model on someone else's machine.

  * The upstream tests are not vendored: they require
    github.com/stretchr/testify, and the conformance suite shells out to a real
    git binary. read_test.go covers the reader and pins the matcher behavior
    Strument relies on, including the ** cases that motivated taking the v6
    matcher over the older, simpler one in v5.

The vendored files are kept in upstream style and excluded from Strument's
linters and formatters, like internal/readline; go vet and go test still cover
them. read.go and read_test.go are Strument's own and are linted normally.
